course: dictionary
lesson: 15405
title: Spotless and what it means
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for spotless. The first is completely clean, with no dirt or marks. «After the cleaners left, the bathroom was spotless.» The clue is that the cleaners have just worked hard, so spotless must mean very clean.
explain: The second meaning is about mistakes. «Sam has a spotless record: he has never broken a rule at school.» Record here means the story of what someone has done. There is no spot or dirt, so spotless means no mistakes or faults. Ask yourself: is this about something dirty, or about something done wrong?
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. Try "completely clean" in place of spotless. If it still makes sense, you have probably found the right meaning.
fact: «Spotless» means completely clean, without any dirt or marks.
fact: «Spotless» can also mean without any mistake or fault, as in «a spotless record».
fact: The adverb is «spotlessly», as in «spotlessly clean».
fact: Hospitals and restaurants must keep their rooms spotless so that they are safe and healthy.
fact: Clues near the word often help, such as «scrubbed», «polished» or «cleaned». A clue like «never broken a rule» points to the second meaning.
exercise: «After the cleaners left, the bathroom was spotless.» What does spotless mean here? | *Completely clean, with no dirt or marks | Full of spots and stains | Noisy and busy | Very dark and dusty
exercise: «Sam has a spotless record: he has never broken a rule at school.» What does spotless record mean? | *No mistakes or faults at all | A very long list of rules | A record of the weather | A record covered in spots
exercise: Mum said, «Keep the kitchen spotless.» Find and copy the word that means clean with no marks. | keep | said | *spotless | kitchen
test: «The hospital corridor was kept spotlessly clean.» What does spotlessly mean? | In a rushed and messy way | In a dark and quiet way | *In a completely clean way | In a way that makes people laugh
test: Which phrase means someone has never made a mistake? | a muddy path | *a spotless record | a loud whistle | a broken window
exam: «Everyone agreed that Priya's project was spotless: no mistakes, no smudges and no errors.» Which meaning of spotless fits best here? | *Without any mistakes or faults | Covered in dirt and paint | Hidden behind a door | Very large and heavy
